* ============================================================================
* cnx_persist_proof.dts
*
* Task #31 / XIDX-TXN-02 M2. Does realtime CNX maintenance SURVIVE A CLOSE?
*
* WHY THIS EXISTS
*   M1 gave CnxBackend working upsert/erase, so a REPLACE that moves an indexed
*   value re-places that record in the CNX ordering immediately (regression
*   CNXLIVE). But the maintained permutation lived only in memory: the container
*   on disk still held whatever the last REBUILD wrote, so the correct order was
*   a property of the SESSION, not of the index. Close the table and the ordering
*   silently reverted.
*
*   That is the gap this proof closes. CNXLIVE asks "is the order right now?".
*   This asks "is it still right after the process stopped looking?" -- which is
*   a DIFFERENT question, against a different capability (IIndexBackend::save,
*   not maintainsIncrementally), and it needs its own proof for exactly the
*   reason the two capabilities were separated in the first place.
*
* WHAT THE MECHANISM IS, SO A FAILURE CAN BE READ
*   save() is append-and-switch: mark CNX_HDRF_DIRTY, append a fresh RUN1 block
*   per mutated tag, then write the tag directory. The directory write is the
*   single commit point. So the interesting failure modes are:
*
*     P2 .F. and no [CNX SAVE] line   -> save never fired. Look at close().
*     P2 .F. and a [CNX SAVE] line    -> it wrote, and the reopen did not see it.
*                                        Look at the tag directory, not the block.
*     [CNX DIRTY] on the reopen       -> the directory write did not land, and
*                                        the recovery path caught it. That is the
*                                        backstop working, not a pass.
*
* MARKER DESIGN
*   Inherited from CNXLIVE/IDXSTALE/CNXBUF and load-bearing for the same reason:
*   every marker is a FIELD comparison. RECNO() and FOUND() render EMPTY in a "?"
*   marker and STR() does not rescue them. Park the cursor on a known different
*   record before any seek, then assert the field value moved.
*
* WHAT THIS PROOF DOES NOT COVER
*   Crash recovery. Setting CNX_HDRF_DIRTY requires interrupting a save between
*   the append and the directory write, which a .dts cannot do. The recovery path
*   is exercised from the host by flipping the flag byte in the header and
*   reopening -- see the session notes. Until that is run, "[CNX DIRTY] triggers
*   a rebuild" is source-evidenced only, and this script must not be read as
*   proving it.
*
*   Durability here means PROCESS death, not power loss: cnxfile has no fsync.
*
* Self-contained: builds and erases its own throwaway v32 table; never touches
* STUDENTS or any live fixture.
*   Standalone:  DOTSCRIPT scripts/cnx_persist_proof.dts
*   Capture:     SET ALTERNATE TO <file> / SET ALTERNATE ON  (never DOTSCRIPT OUT)
*
* Runtime status: GREEN 2026-08-01, wsl-lean, 11/11 markers. [CNX SAVE] fired
*   once at the first CLOSE (root=4240) and NOT at the second, which is P8's
*   real evidence. Lane record: XIDX_TXN_02_PDLC_LANE_V1.md (M2).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

* x32 lane: CNX is the v32 indexing backend
DO x32

FORMULA "CNX-PERSIST-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- fixture: throwaway v32 table, CNX order on LNAME -------------------------
ERASE TABLE CNXPERS CONFIRM
CREATE CNXPERS (SID N(8), LNAME C(20))

APPEND
REPLACE SID WITH 1
REPLACE LNAME WITH "MILLER"
APPEND
REPLACE SID WITH 2
REPLACE LNAME WITH "ANDERSON"
APPEND
REPLACE SID WITH 3
REPLACE LNAME WITH "ZEBRA"
APPEND
REPLACE SID WITH 4
REPLACE LNAME WITH "YOUNG"

CNX CREATE
CNX ADDTAG LNAME
REBUILD
SET ORDER TAG LNAME

* --- P_G0/P_G1: fixture guards ----------------------------------------------
* If either fails, everything below is meaningless.
GO 4
SEEK "MILLER"
? "P_G0_seek_works_before_edit:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "MILLER")

GO TOP
? "P_G1_baseline_top_is_ANDERSON:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ANDERSON")

* ============================================================================
* PART 1 -- the M1 precondition: maintained in memory
* ============================================================================
* Not the point of this proof, but if this is already wrong then P2 would be
* testing persistence of a WRONG ordering, which would look like a pass for the
* wrong reason. Assert the starting state is correct before persisting it.
GO 1
REPLACE LNAME WITH "AAAAA"

GO TOP
? "P1_maintained_in_memory_top_is_AAAAA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "AAAAA")

* ============================================================================
* PART 2 -- THE MILESTONE: does it survive the close?
* ============================================================================
* CLOSE is the trigger. CnxBackend::close() saves before clearing, so the
* container should carry the maintained permutation from here on.
*
* NO REBUILD ANYWHERE BELOW. That is the whole assertion: a rebuild would
* reconstruct the correct order from the table and prove nothing about whether
* the save happened.
CLOSE

USE CNXPERS
SET ORDER TAG LNAME

GO TOP
? "P2_survives_close_top_is_AAAAA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "AAAAA")

* --- P3: the rest of the ordering came back too ------------------------------
* A save that wrote only the moved record, or truncated the block, would still
* pass P2. Check both interior and tail.
GO TOP
SKIP
? "P3_second_is_ANDERSON:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ANDERSON")

BOTTOM
? "P4_bottom_is_ZEBRA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ZEBRA")

* --- P5: lookup agrees with the persisted order ------------------------------
* Park somewhere else first so a stale cursor cannot fake this.
GO 3
SEEK "AAAAA"
? "P5_seek_reaches_moved_record:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "AAAAA")

* ============================================================================
* PART 3 -- the persisted order must AGREE WITH A REBUILD
* ============================================================================
* The strongest assertion here, and the same shape as CNXLIVE L_T6 and CNXBUF
* B5. If save() wrote a permutation that differs from what the table implies,
* the order CHANGES across this line and every earlier marker was measuring a
* consistent lie. The rebuild must be a no-op.
REBUILD
SET ORDER TAG LNAME

GO TOP
? "P6_rebuild_agrees_with_persisted:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "AAAAA")

BOTTOM
? "P7_rebuild_agrees_at_tail:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ZEBRA")

* ============================================================================
* PART 4 -- a second close with no edits must not corrupt anything
* ============================================================================
* Idempotence. save() is called on every close, and both a close-time and a
* commit-time save can fire for one edit, so saving twice with nothing owed has
* to be harmless. dirty_tags_ is empty here, so save() should return success
* without opening the file at all -- externally visible as the ABSENCE of a
* second [CNX SAVE] line for this tag.
CLOSE

USE CNXPERS
SET ORDER TAG LNAME

GO TOP
? "P8_idempotent_close_top_is_AAAAA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "AAAAA")

BOTTOM
? "P9_idempotent_close_tail_is_ZEBRA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ZEBRA")

FORMULA "CNX-PERSIST-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown ----------------------------------------------------------------
CLOSE
ERASE TABLE CNXPERS CONFIRM
